WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.660
Hi everyone.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.480
So, as a data engineer, I’ve had a few job interviews,

3
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.180
and one thing I’ve learned

4
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.620
is that asking questions is just as important as answering them.

5
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.300
First of all, before going to an interview,

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.420
I always try to learn more about the company,

7
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.660
its projects and the technologies they use.

8
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.620
Then, during the interview, I like to ask questions such as:

9
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.940
“What are the main data challenges your team is currently facing?”

10
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:35.000
or “What tools and technologies do you use for your data pipelines?”

11
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.280
Also, I think it’s really important to ask about training programmes

12
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.260
and opportunities to get certifications.

13
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.360
Why? Well, because in the data field,

14
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.600
technologies are constantly changing and there is always something new to learn.

15
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.320
Another question I find really useful is:

16
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.980
“What would you expect from me during my first three months?”

17
00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:03.240
Actually, I think these kinds of questions helped me understand the position better,

18
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.780
get to know the team and see if the company matches my professional goals.

19
00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:13.060
And of course, I also try to listen carefully during the interview,

20
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.670
because I don’t want to ask something that has already been explained.

21
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.620
Finally, at the end of the interview,

22
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.600
I always thank the interviewers for their time

23
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.880
and ask about the next steps in the recruitment process.

24
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:35.320
So, to sum up, I believe that a job interview is a two-way conversation.

25
00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.860
It’s not only about the company deciding whether you’re the right person for the job,

26
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:46.380
but also about you seeing whether the company is the right place for you.

27
00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:52.150
And that’s why I think asking the right questions can really make a difference.
